From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: keys OmacVM's helpers post for macOS never go to the guest

What: a key event marked with OmacVM's marker (kCGEventSourceUserData =
0x0BAC0E5C, the value OmacVM Bridge already marks its own posted keys with)
is not the guest's: QEMU's full-grab tap lets it through and the app does
not send it to the VM.

Why: after Ctrl+Option+Cmd+Esc, OmacVM Gestures leaves the VM's full-screen
Space with macOS's own "Move left/right a space" shortcut (Ctrl+Left/Right
by default), posted at the HID level. QEMU's window is still key at that
moment, so its full-grab tap (qemu-cocoa-full-grab-focus.patch) took the
shortcut and typed Ctrl+Left into Omarchy; macOS never saw it. The user
wants to swipe away to macOS, not leave full screen (Mac mini, macOS 27,
2026-10-05: the synthesized Dock swipe does nothing there).

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's helpers).
Test: src/gestures/mac/test.sh checks that Gestures, the Bridge and this
patch use the same marker; the build checks the patch is in ui/cocoa.m.
The escape path itself: src/gestures/mac/test-escape.c (no QEMU).

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -649,7 +649,27 @@
     [cocoaView resetPinchLocked:running];
 }
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM: a key that OmacVM's Mac helpers post for macOS itself carries this
+ * value in kCGEventSourceUserData (the Bridge's marker; OmacVM Gestures posts
+ * macOS's "Move left/right a space" shortcut with it after the escape combo).
+ * It never goes to the guest, even while our window has the keyboard, so
+ * macOS gets it.
+ */
+#define OMACVM_MAC_KEY_MARKER 0x0BAC0E5C
 
+static bool omacvm_key_for_macos(NSEvent *event)
+{
+    NSEventType type = [event type];
+    if (!event || (type != NSEventTypeKeyDown && type != NSEventTypeKeyUp &&
+                   type != NSEventTypeFlagsChanged)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    CGEventRef cgEvent = [event CGEvent];
+    return cgEvent && CGEventGetIntegerValueField(cgEvent, kCGEventSourceUserData) ==
+                      OMACVM_MAC_KEY_MARKER;
+}
+
 static CGEventRef handleTapEvent(CGEventTapProxy proxy, CGEventType type, CGEventRef cgEvent, void *userInfo)
 {
     QemuCocoaView *view = userInfo;
@@ -1335,6 +1355,9 @@
 
 - (bool) handleEvent:(NSEvent *)event
 {
+    if (omacvm_key_for_macos(event)) {
+        return false;
+    }
     return bool_with_bql(^{
         return [self handleEventLocked:event];
     });
